      "description": "Brightspeed owns and operates wireline telecommunications and fiber broadband infrastructure across 20 U.S. states from Charlotte, North Carolina. Apollo-managed funds completed the acquisition of Lumen's incumbent local exchange carrier operations in October 2022. The FCC's 2022 approval order for the subsequently consummated acquisition shows that the Apollo ownership group included AIOF II Connect Holdings, L.P., a vehicle of Apollo Infrastructure Opportunities Fund II, with a direct interest of less than 5% alongside larger Apollo private-equity and co-invest vehicles; the 2% equity and 3% voting values appeared only in the December 2023 proposed post-Mubadala structure. Mubadala signed a $500 million minority investment through CEPSA Holding LLC in May 2023, and the FCC approved the proposed foreign-ownership structure in December 2023; no public legal-closing announcement or date was found, so Mubadala remains a signed pending incoming investor in this census. Brightspeed completed a debt recapitalization in August 2024 that issued warrants and preferred stock, and the current exact ownership percentages are not publicly disclosed. No Apollo or Mubadala exit was found through August 8, 2026.",
